#
# OCI 11.2's data-type request to 10g (#2518): 11g's (encode_dty_oci11), but
# without the timezone-file version, the big-endian ub4 14 behind the time-zone
# block: 67 bytes, against 71 to 11g.
# Captured 2026-11-08 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, the client charset AL32UTF8, called
# through ctypes) on Oracle 10g 10.2.0.5, a dedicated session. The TTC payload,
# without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the
# |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
00000000  02 69 03 69 03 83 27 06  01 01 01 0f 01 01 06 01  |.i.i..'.........|
00000010  01 01 01 01 01 01 7f ff  03 0a 03 07 01 01 7f 01  |................|
00000020  7f ff 01 09 01 01 bf 01  05 06 00 01 07 04 07 02  |................|
00000030  01 00 00 18 00 03 80 00  00 00 3c 3c 3c 80 00 00  |..........<<<...|
00000040  00 d0 07                                          |...|
00000043
